{"id":766,"name":"Central Sikhote-Alin","category":"Natural","danger":false,"year":2001,"countries":"Russian Federation","transboundary":false,"criteria":"(x)","description":"Central Sikhote-Alin protects forested mountains in Russia's Far East, running inland from the Pacific coast north of Vladivostok. Here the northern taiga meets the warmer south, so Amur tigers and Himalayan bears share woodland with brown bears, lynx, wolverines and sable. A later addition brought in the remote Bikin River Valley, roughly 100 km farther north.","description_generated":true,"image":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%D0%93%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%8B_%D0%A1%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%B3%D0%BE_%D0%A1%D0%B8%D1%85%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%8D-%D0%90%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%8F%2C_%D0%BE%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B5_%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%83%D1%82%D1%8B%D0%B5_%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B8.jpg?width=800","image_page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%93%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%8B_%D0%A1%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%B3%D0%BE_%D0%A1%D0%B8%D1%85%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%8D-%D0%90%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%8F%2C_%D0%BE%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B5_%D0%BD%D0%B5%D1%82%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%BD%D1%83%D1%82%D1%8B%D0%B5_%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%82%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B8.jpg","unesco_url":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/766/","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sikhote-Alin","wikidata_url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q64787152"}